If you are wielding Magicbane, the CoMR is not mandatory.
A robe will allow you to cast FoD with ease. Grease it if possible.
Priests almost always have robes, and you are chaotic, so you can
pick one up in minetown, at the very least.

Ditch the iron shoes (elvin boots should be easy to find), and replace
the dwarvish helm with a elvin leather helm, cornuthaum, or HoB.

If you have a magic marker and max out your luck, you can write almost
any spell.  Also, force-bolt all statues to find more spellbooks.

Once you enhance divination to skilled, you get truly useful detect
monsters.

Stone-to-flesh can be very useful for getting your level high enough
to go on the quest - you can kill Medusa dozens of times.  Once on the
quest, use stealth to approach the Dark One and finger him from a
distance before he picks up the Eye.  Once you have the Eye, your fast
mana regen will make you a much more effective spellcaster.

If you want to polypile your way to spellbook completion, bless the
spellbook of polymorph, read it, and wear a robe and no metal armor
(except HoB) to cast it.
Hang on to the spellbooks that you will want to re-read, bless and
polypile the rest. Use 3 or 4 small piles.

